{"name":"Rural Red","hex":"#bb1144","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rural","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Relating to the countryside or to agriculture."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person from the countryside; a rustic."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rural"},{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rural area","blocks":[{"text":"A rural area, also known as the country or countryside, is a geographic area that is located outside towns and cities. Typical rural areas have a low population density and small settlements. Agricultural areas and areas with forestry are typically described as rural, as well as other areas lacking substantial development. Different countries have varying definitions of rural for statistical and administrative purposes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Joshua_Shaw_-_%27View_in_the_Pennsylvania_Countryside%27%2C_1823.JPG/330px-Joshua_Shaw_-_%27View_in_the_Pennsylvania_Countryside%27%2C_1823.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rural_area"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Baling_hay_in_Vermont.jpg/500px-Baling_hay_in_Vermont.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Baling_hay_in_Vermont.jpg/1280px-Baling_hay_in_Vermont.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Baling_hay_in_Vermont.jpg/500px-Baling_hay_in_Vermont.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Westminster, Vermont","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABaling_hay_in_Vermont.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Indiana-rural-road.jpg/500px-Indiana-rural-road.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Indiana-rural-road.jpg/1280px-Indiana-rural-road.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Indiana-rural-road.jpg/500px-Indiana-rural-road.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A rural country road in Marshall County, Indiana","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIndiana-rural-road.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Mount_Shasta_%281%29.jpg/500px-Mount_Shasta_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.or